# Holzen — context before you change code

Non-trivial work should be **classified** against the **Change map** table in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) (section **Change map (read this before non-trivial edits)**). Open the **Read first** link for your slice before editing.

## Invariants (do not drop on “small” PRs)

- **Product analytics:** new or renamed PostHog events/properties → update [docs/ops/event-taxonomy.md](../../docs/ops/event-taxonomy.md) in the same PR.
- **Feature flags:** new or materially changed flag → update [docs/ops/feature-flags.md](../../docs/ops/feature-flags.md) in the same PR.
- **Edge HTTP surface:** new function or entrypoint → `supabase/config.toml` `[functions.*]`, `EdgeCoverage.tsx`, and logging checks per [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) commands + `.cursor/rules/deployment-sync.mdc`.
- **DB migrations:** follow [docs/ops/migration-security-conventions.md](../../docs/ops/migration-security-conventions.md); views → [docs/ops/migration-view-safety.md](../../docs/ops/migration-view-safety.md).
- **Correlation:** new `functions.invoke` / edge calls → keep **`x-cid`** via `invokeEdge` or `withCidHeaders()` (see AGENTS **Cross-surface correlation**).

## Full index

- [docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md) — start-here order and **canonical sources** (single owner per kind of information).
- Incremental `src/` migration sessions: [.cursor/rules/architecture-migration.mdc](architecture-migration.mdc), [pause-client-architecture.md](../../docs/systems/pause-client-architecture.md), [implementation-notes-workflow.md](../../docs/fundamentals/implementation-notes-workflow.md), live [implementation-notes.html](../../docs/artifacts/architecture-migration/implementation-notes.html).
- Flow-first review templates: [docs/reviews/react-spa-review-template.md](../../docs/reviews/react-spa-review-template.md), skill `holzen-flow-review`.

If a doc and code disagree, **fix the doc in the same PR** when you changed behavior—or file a tiny follow-up only when scope is intentionally split.
